      "content": "When traditional fixes feel ineffective, it suggests the issue might be deeper than just scheduling or taking a break. This feeling of hitting a conclusive wall can be profoundly heavy, and it’s okay to feel exhausted by the whole pursuit of \"fixing\" it. Instead of viewing therapy as another obligation, perhaps explore low-stakes ways to reconnect with genuine self-interest, even if they feel small. Remember that a loved one or doctor can be a starting point if formal therapy feels too much right now.",
